## 3. Design Rationale

### Zero-copy strategy
- Unescaped strings are returned as `std::string_view` pointing directly into the caller's input buffer — zero allocation, zero copying.
- Only strings containing escapes (`\" \\ \/ \b \f \n \r \t \uXXXX`) are decoded into the arena via `MemoryPool::allocate_copy`.
- Numbers are parsed in place with a hand-rolled scanner (no `strtod` locale overhead; fast-path integer detection).

### Memory pool arena
- Bump-pointer allocation: `allocate()` is a pointer bump plus alignment fix-up — O(1) and cache-friendly.
- Fixed 64 KiB blocks; a new block is added only when the current one is exhausted, so large documents amortize to a handful of blocks.
- `reset()` rewinds all block offsets in O(block_count) — ideal for server-style parse loops.
- All AST nodes, array/object slices, and unescaped strings live in the arena; the whole tree is freed with one `reset()`.

### AST layout
- `JsonValue` is 32 bytes on 64-bit platforms (tag + union), enabling tight array packing.
- Arrays are contiguous `JsonValue` slices; objects are contiguous `[key, value]` pairs for cache-friendly linear scans and optional key sorting.

### Error reporting
- Every error carries byte offset plus 1-based line/column, computed incrementally during scanning (no second pass).
- Depth guard prevents stack exhaustion on adversarial nesting.

### CMake build graph
- Header-only `devbench_json` interface target for maximum inlining (parser hot paths).
- Optional static library `devbench_json_static` for ABI-stable linking and benchmarks.
- Strict warnings (`-Wall -Wextra -Wpedantic -Wconversion -Wshadow`), Release `-O3 -march=native`, optional ASan/UBSan in Debug.
- `tests/` subdirectory wired via `add_subdirectory` for the unit-test phase.

